# Declare a Prompt card

## Prerequisites

- Wyrd set up from a repo checkout ([Get started](/get-started/))

## Recipe

```python
from pathlib import Path

from wyrd import Prompt
from wyrd.prompt import PromptCard

prompt = Prompt(
    provider="openai",
    model="gpt-4o-mini",
    messages=["Summarise the following document in {max_words} words:\n\n{document}"],
)

card = PromptCard(
    prompt,
    name="summarise-document",
    version="0.1.0",
)

card.save(Path("./summarise-prompt"))
```

The first positional argument is a `Prompt` — the provider, model, and messages
live on it. The `PromptCard` wraps it with identity (`name`, `version`, and a
`space` that defaults to `default`).

`card.save(path)` writes the local card layout. Registration to a server is the
HTTP route `POST /api/v1/cards` (see [Declare a Data card](/how-to/declare/data/)
for the request shape); there is no Python registry client yet.

## Notes

- Keep `name` stable — downstream agents, policies, and audits refer to it by
  identity.
- `version` follows semver. The server rejects a changed spec at the same version.
- Provider settings can be pinned with the `model_settings` argument to
  `PromptCard`.

